     "text": "**Why the Eigenfunction Method Fails**:\nAn eigenfunction of an LTI system must satisfy $y[n] = \\lambda x[n]$ for all $n$.\nHere, $x[n] = 0$ for $n < 0$. If $x[n]$ were an eigenfunction, $y[n]$ would also have to be identical to $2^n u[n]$ scaled by a constant. But convolution of two causal signals produces transients for $n \\ge 0$. Thus, $2^n u[n]$ is **not** an eigenfunction!"
