     "t": "code",
     "text": "+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  PAGE 18 - BOTTOM RIGHT (SLIDE 072)                                      |\n|                                                                          |\n|  Q.            e^{j\\omega_0 n} ---->[ H(e^{j\\omega}) ]----> y[n]         |\n|                = (z_0)^n                                                 |\n|                z_0 = e^{j\\omega_0}, |z_0| = 1                            |\n|                H(e^{j\\omega}) is defined \\implies |z_0| = 1 lies in ROC   |\n|                                                                          |\n|                +------------------------------------+                    |\n|                | y[n] = e^{j\\omega_0 n} H(e^{j\\omega_0}) |               |\n|                +------------------------------------+                    |\n|                                                                          |\n|  Q.  x[n] = 3 e^{j(\\frac{\\pi}{2}n + \\frac{\\pi}{3})}                      |\n|      H(e^{j\\omega}) = \\frac{1}{1 - \\frac{1}{2}e^{-j\\omega}}              |\n|                                                                          |\n|      y[n] = 3 e^{j(\\frac{\\pi}{2}n + \\frac{\\pi}{3})} H(e^{j\\pi/2})        |\n|           = 3 e^{j(\\frac{\\pi}{2}n + \\frac{\\pi}{3})} \\frac{1}{1 - \\frac{1}{2} e^{-j\\pi/2}}|\n|           = 3 e^{j(\\frac{\\pi}{2}n + \\frac{\\pi}{3})} \\left(\\frac{2}{2+j}\\right) Ans. |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+"
