     "text": "+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  PAGE 19 - TOP LEFT (SLIDE 073)                                          |\n|                                                                          |\n|  Q.          \\cos(\\omega_0 n) ---->[ H(e^{j\\omega}) ]----> y[n]          |\n|              = \\frac{e^{j\\omega_0 n} + e^{-j\\omega_0 n}}{2}              |\n|                                                                          |\n|      y[n] = \\frac{1}{2} e^{j\\omega_0 n} H(e^{j\\omega_0}) + \\frac{1}{2} e^{-j\\omega_0 n} H(e^{-j\\omega_0})|\n|                                                                          |\n|      If  H(e^{j\\omega_0}) = H(e^{-j\\omega_0}) = H(e^{j\\omega_0})         |\n|                                                                          |\n|      y[n] = H(e^{j\\omega_0}) \\left[ \\frac{e^{j\\omega_0 n} + e^{-j\\omega_0 n}}{2} \\right]|\n|                                                                          |\n|      +-----------------------------------------+                         |\n|      | y[n] = \\cos(\\omega_0 n) \\cdot H(e^{j\\omega_0}) |                  |\n|      +-----------------------------------------+                         |\n|                 ^                   ^                                    |\n|              Eigen fn           Eigen value                              |\n|                                                                          |\n|      +---------------------------------------------------------+         |\n|      | \\cos(\\omega_0 n) will be an eigen fn to a stable LTI     |         |\n|      | s/s ONLY WHEN  H(e^{j\\omega_0}) = H(e^{-j\\omega_0})     |         |\n|      +---------------------------------------------------------+         |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+"
