     "t": "code",
     "text": "+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  PAGE 19 - BOTTOM LEFT (SLIDE 075)                                       |\n|                                                                          |\n|  * For a stable LTI s/s: (ROC includes |z|=1 circle \\implies H(e^{j\\omega}) def)|\n|                                                                          |\n|    (\\checkmark) (a) A e^{j(\\omega_0 n + \\phi)} is ALWAYS an eigen fn.    |\n|                                                                          |\n|    (\\checkmark) (b) A \\cos(\\omega_0 n + \\phi) and A \\sin(\\omega_0 n + \\phi)|\n|                     are NOT the eigen fn always.                         |\n|                                                                          |\n|    (\\checkmark) (c) A \\cos(\\omega_0 n + \\phi) and A \\sin(\\omega_0 n + \\phi)|\n|                     ARE eigen fn WHEN  H(e^{j\\omega_0}) = H(e^{-j\\omega_0})|\n|                                                                          |\n|    (\\checkmark) (d) If h[n] -> EVEN, then A \\cos(\\omega_0 n + \\phi)      |\n|                     and A \\sin(\\omega_0 n + \\phi) ARE eigen functions.   |\n|                                                                          |\n|                     H(e^{j\\omega}) = H(e^{-j\\omega}) <--- h[n] = h[-n]   |\n|                     \\implies H(e^{j\\omega_0}) = H(e^{-j\\omega_0})        |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+"
